---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { tree } from '../../lib/tree';

const systemTiers = tree.tiers.filter((t) => t.group === 'system');
const accessTiers = tree.tiers.filter((t) => t.group === 'access');
const c = tree.counts;
const plainFactor = tree.factors.filter((f) => f.letter !== 'C');
const contact = tree.factors.find((f) => f.letter === 'C');
---

<Base title="What has to happen — The Belt Equation" description="Every event the Belt Equation tracks, with a test for whether it has happened, and the milestones that define what 'human industry reaches beyond Earth and Mars' and 'live and work off Earth' mean.">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">The tree</p>
    <h1>{c.nodes} things that have to happen, and a test for each</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The number on the home page is built from {c.nodes} events: breakthroughs, decisions, and milestones.
      Each one has a plain name and a written test, so that anyone can check later whether it happened, with no judgment call.
      If an event can't be tested that way, it doesn't get in.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <ul class="tally">
      <li><span class="stat">{c.leaves}</span><span class="stat-label">could be decided either way by 2031</span></li>
      <li><span class="stat">{c.resolved}</span><span class="stat-label">already happened</span></li>
      <li><span class="stat">{c.long_shots}</span><span class="stat-label">deliberate long shots, kept on the board because they make the goal vivid</span></li>
      <li><span class="stat">{c.choice_points}</span><span class="stat-label">are my own decisions, not things that happen to the world</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shead"><h2>For human industry to reach beyond Earth and Mars</h2><span>four milestones, each building on the last</span></div>
    <p class="section-note">The Expanse is a story. To say whether it is coming true, the project uses four milestones, from a first permanent base to millions living out there with their own economy and politics. Each milestone is a short list of events that all have to happen. The third one, Slow Expanse, is the bar the headline is counted against: human industry reaching beyond Earth and Mars.</p>
    <div class="grid-2">
      {systemTiers.map((t, i) => (
        <div class={`rail ${t.key === 'T3' ? 'marked' : ''}`}>
          <h4><span class="step">{i + 1}</span> {t.name}{t.key === 'T3' ? ' · the bar' : ''}</h4>
          <p class="rail-def">{t.definition}</p>
          <p class="rail-req">Needs:</p>
          <ul>
            {t.requires.map((r) => (
              <li>{r.kind === 'tier'
                ? <span class="dim">everything in {r.name}</span>
                : <a href={`/tree/${r.factor_slug}/${r.id}/`}>{r.name}</a>}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shead"><h2>For me to live and work out there</h2><span>four rungs, from contributing on Earth to living out there</span></div>
    <p class="section-note">"Live and work off Earth" could mean a lot of things, so the project spells out four rungs. The headline number on the home page is the third rung: working off Earth for months at a time. The fourth, living there permanently, is reported beside it as the stretch.</p>
    <div class="grid-2">
      {accessTiers.map((t, i) => (
        <div class={`rail ${t.key === tree.headline_tier ? 'marked' : ''}`}>
          <h4><span class="step">{i + 1}</span> {t.name}{t.key === tree.headline_tier ? ' · the headline' : ''}</h4>
          <p class="rail-def">{t.definition}</p>
          <p class="rail-req">Needs:</p>
          <ul>
            {t.requires.map((r) => (
              <li>{r.kind === 'tier'
                ? <span class="dim">everything in {r.name}</span>
                : <a href={`/tree/${r.factor_slug}/${r.id}/`}>{r.name}</a>}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="picture">
    <div class="shead"><h2>The whole tree as one picture</h2><span>every event, coloured by link, arrows from what it needs</span></div>
    <p class="section-note">Three columns by how soon an event could be decided (within five years, within twenty, or only over a lifetime), rows grouped by link. Each box carries the event's chance by 2071, by 2095 and with no deadline, given what it depends on. Dashed boxes are my own decisions; filled boxes have already happened. It is drawn from the same tree and the same run as every number on this site, so it cannot disagree with them. <a href="/tree.svg">Open it full size</a>.</p>
    <a class="picture" href="/tree.svg" aria-label="The whole tree as one picture, full size">
      <img src="/tree.svg" alt="The Belt Equation's tree: every event as a box coloured by link, with arrows from each event to the events that need it, and the headline numbers in a box at the top" loading="lazy" />
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shead"><h2>All {c.nodes} events, by link</h2><span>the seven links from the home page, and the one beside them</span></div>
    <p class="section-note">Every event belongs to one of the seven links in the chain. Open a link to see its events, each with its test, its current probability, and what it depends on.</p>
    <div class="fgrid">
      {plainFactor.map((f) => (
        <a class="fcard" href={f.path}>
          <span class="fletter">{f.letter}</span>
          <h3>{f.name}</h3>
          <p>{f.meaning}</p>
          <p class="fcount">{f.node_count} events · {f.with_probability} with a number{f.resolved ? ` · ${f.resolved} already happened` : ''}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
      {contact && (
        <a class="fcard contact" href={contact.path}>
          <span class="fletter">Beside the chain</span>
          <h3>{contact.name}</h3>
          <p>{contact.meaning}</p>
          <p class="fcount">{contact.node_count} events · {contact.with_probability} with a number · never multiplied in</p>
        </a>
      )}
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
